p tells you what matters, not what is true. Existing C helps avoid duplicates. Extract 0–3 NEW factual findings across this acquisition only when the observations directly support the full statement, materially advance this OneGap, and add facts not already adequately represented in C. If none, return findings=[].\"\n\nObservation doesn't directly support any of the OneGap elements. So findings likely [].\n\nNeed ensure no general facts. Return {\"findings\":[]}.\n\nBut maybe there is a finding: \"Autar Krishen Rehbar has proved that the basic lines of a poem are that of Arinimaal only, and that it is distinct from the poem attributed to Mehmud Gaami except for a common refrain.\" This is factual, new, but does it materially advance OneGap? OneGap about birth dates, chronology, husband. No.\n\nWhat about \"This poem was not attached to Arinimaal as late as 1946\" might imply attribution late, but not birth. Not OneGap.\n\nThus findings empty."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":953,"completion_tokens":645,"total_tokens":1598,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":638},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":953},"system_fingerprint":"aeb56401ca74e127821c4f9126dcb669"}